From b59705b26b0c759eceba14e65223c2f61961932f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:37:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: skip ACPI DSM without an ACPI companion
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rtw89 asks for optional regulatory and SAR policy through an ACPI _DSM even
when its device was enumerated without an ACPI companion.  Passing a NULL
handle to the ACPI evaluator emits misleading errors on Device Tree
systems.  The driver then correctly falls back to its default policy.

Check for an ACPI handle before evaluating the method.  Return the result
used when the optional method is unavailable.  This retains the fallback
behavior without invoking an inapplicable firmware API.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c
@@ -372,11 +372,14 @@ int rtw89_acpi_evaluate_dsm(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
 			    enum rtw89_acpi_dsm_func func,
 			    struct rtw89_acpi_dsm_result *res)
 {
+	acpi_handle handle = ACPI_HANDLE(rtwdev->dev);
 	union acpi_object *obj;
 	int ret;
 
-	obj = acpi_evaluate_dsm(ACPI_HANDLE(rtwdev->dev), &rtw89_guid,
-				0, func, NULL);
+	if (!handle)
+		return -ENOENT;
+
+	obj = acpi_evaluate_dsm(handle, &rtw89_guid, 0, func, NULL);
 	if (!obj) {
 		rtw89_debug(rtwdev, RTW89_DBG_ACPI,
 			    "acpi dsm fail to evaluate func: %d\n", func);
-- 
